{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the cities, etc., the six cities of refuge.</b> From here it appears that the six cities of refuge are for the exiles and not for the Levites. And from his statement in the verse that follows this one, where he said <b>all the cities which you shall give to the Levites are forty-eight</b>, it appears that the six as well are for the privilege of the Levites. And it appears that the verse intended by this to grant equal privilege to the Israelites who are exiled and to the Levites, so that the hand of all of them is equal. Therefore in the first verse he stated a privilege for the exiles, that the six cities of refuge should be for them to dwell in, and in the second verse he gave the privilege to the Levites — from this you learn that they belong to the Levites and they belong to the exiles, and the exiles do not pay rent, and so they concluded at the end of [the chapter on] the exiles (Makkot 13a) according to all the opinions. And I am inclined to say that a Levite is displaced on account of an Israelite exile: if the killers multiplied and all six cities were needed, the Levites would be displaced from them, for the verse gave precedence to the privilege of the exiles."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:16.163387965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}